# Module: Agreement

## Agreement-UC1 — View Agreement Details

- Primary Actor(s): User
- Secondary Actor(s): None
- Trigger: User requests to view agreement details.
- Description: This use case allows a user to view the details of an agreement.
- Preconditions:
  - User has access to the application.
  - Agreement exists in the system.
- Postconditions:
  - The user is displayed the detailed information of the specified agreement.
- Main Success Scenario:
  1. User selects an agreement to view.
  2. System retrieves and displays agreement details including type, description, last updated, and status.
- Extensions:
  - None.
- Exceptions:
  - Agreement does not exist.
- Business Rules:
  - Display agreement details only to authorized users.
- Assumptions:
  - User has the necessary permissions.
- Open Issues:
  - None.

## Agreement-UC2 — Add New Agreement

- Primary Actor(s): Admin
- Secondary Actor(s): None
- Trigger: Admin initiates the process to add a new agreement.
- Description: Admin can create a new agreement entry in the system.
- Preconditions:
  - Admin has appropriate permissions.
- Postconditions:
  - A new agreement is added and assigned an ID.
- Main Success Scenario:
  1. Admin selects the option to add a new agreement.
  2. Admin enters necessary agreement details.
  3. System validates and saves the new agreement.
- Extensions:
  - If template is used, apply the relevant details.
- Exceptions:
  - Validation fails due to missing information.
- Business Rules:
  - All required fields must be filled.
- Assumptions:
  - Admin has all necessary details to create the agreement.
- Open Issues:
  - None.

## Agreement-UC3 — Update Existing Agreement

- Primary Actor(s): Admin
- Secondary Actor(s): None
- Trigger: Admin chooses to update an existing agreement.
- Description: Allows updating the details of an existing agreement.
- Preconditions:
  - Agreement exists and admin has permissions.
- Postconditions:
  - Agreement details are updated in the system.
- Main Success Scenario:
  1. Admin selects an agreement to update.
  2. Admin modifies necessary fields.
  3. System validates and saves the updated details.
- Extensions:
  - None.
- Exceptions:
  - Errors in data validation.
- Business Rules:
  - Only editable fields can be modified.
- Assumptions:
  - Admin inputs valid data.
- Open Issues:
  - None.

## Agreement-UC4 — Delete Agreement

- Primary Actor(s): Admin
- Secondary Actor(s): None
- Trigger: Admin opts to delete an agreement.
- Description: This use case describes the deletion of an agreement.
- Preconditions:
  - Agreement exists.
- Postconditions:
  - Agreement is marked as deleted.
- Main Success Scenario:
  1. Admin selects an agreement to delete.
  2. System prompts for confirmation.
  3. Admin confirms deletion.
  4. System deletes the agreement.
- Extensions:
  - None.
- Exceptions:
  - Agreement is linked to other records and cannot be deleted.
- Business Rules:
  - Deletion should be confirmed explicitly.
- Assumptions:
  - Admin understands the implications of deletion.
- Open Issues:
  - None.

## Agreement-UC5 — Search for Agreements

- Primary Actor(s): User
- Secondary Actor(s): None
- Trigger: User initiates search for agreements.
- Description: This use case allows users to search agreements by various criteria.
- Preconditions:
  - User has permission to view agreements.
- Postconditions:
  - System displays a list of agreements matching the search criteria.
- Main Success Scenario:
  1. User enters search criteria.
  2. System retrieves agreements matching the criteria.
  3. User views the list of results.
- Extensions:
  - Search results can be sorted by different columns.
- Exceptions:
  - No agreements match the search criteria.
- Business Rules:
  - Search criteria must be valid.
- Assumptions:
  - User inputs accurate criteria.
- Open Issues:
  - None.